        <h2>Do I need to be Peruvian to buy?</h2>
        <p>No. Foreigners buy property in Peru. There is a serious limit within 50 km of the borders, and residency is a separate question. I bought before I was a citizen and again after.</p>
        <h2>Does buying give me residency?</h2>
        <p>No. See <a href="residency.html">residency</a>.</p>
        <h2>Can I buy without visiting?</h2>
        <p>Yes, with scouting, a lawyer, and a tightly scoped <span lang="es">poder</span>. It is still better to visit, or to rent in the area for a few months. I can help arrange the rental.</p>
        <h2>Is a few thousand dollars a real budget?</h2>
        <p>For an 8×20 meter lot in some provincial places, yes, that is a kind of purchase I can help with. It is not a budget for a finished house in Miraflores, and the cheap lot still needs a reality check on title, services, and what building costs in kind.</p>
        <h2>Can you help with a large forest parcel?</h2>
        <p>Yes, on the order of large agricultural or forest land, up to about 100 hectares as a scale I am willing to talk about. Title, access, water, community land, and the border zone matter more, not less.</p>
        <h2>Will I make a profit if I sell?</h2>
        <p>Not as a promise. I have bought and sold for a profit by knowing price ranges. Values can fall. This is not investment advice.</p>
        <h2>Are you my lawyer?</h2>
        <p>No. Hire your own. I work beside an independent lawyer and a notary. I am not a registered <span lang="es">agente inmobiliario</span> on this site, and I am not your tax advisor.</p>
        <h2>Can you cover all of Peru?</h2>
        <p>No. I scout the places I know. Elsewhere, a trusted local contact walks the property if that is the honest fit.</p>
        <h2>What does a visit report include?</h2>
        <p>The list is on the <a href="scout.html">scouting page</a>: different times of day, neighbors, surroundings, condition, boundaries, photos and video.</p>
        <h2>How do fees work?</h2>
        <p>I quote after intake for the service we actually scope. I have not published a commission policy. The packages are listed under <a href="services.html">services</a>.</p>
        <h2>How do we start?</h2>
        <p><a href="contact.html">Send the intake.</a> If you want a first sort without writing, use the <a href="quiz.html">region quiz</a> and read the matching notes.</p>
